From: pulpoff <pashkovsky@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] orientation-manager: Export the tracking inhibit

meta_orientation_manager_inhibit_tracking() and _uninhibit_tracking()
are in the public header, so they are in the typelib, but without
META_EXPORT they are not in libmutter's exported symbols: a call from
the shell fails with "undefined symbol". gnome-phone holds the panel
upright for the lock screen with them, as Android keeps its lock screen
portrait on a phone.

For mutter-mobile 51.1.mobile.22 (/usr/src/gnome-mobile/mutter on the
S10e, built into /opt/gnome-mobile by build51.sh).
---
--- a/src/meta/meta-orientation-manager.h
+++ b/src/meta/meta-orientation-manager.h
@@ -52,6 +52,8 @@
 META_EXPORT
 MtkMonitorTransform meta_orientation_to_transform (MetaOrientation orientation);
 
+META_EXPORT
 void meta_orientation_manager_inhibit_tracking (MetaOrientationManager *self);
 
+META_EXPORT
 void meta_orientation_manager_uninhibit_tracking (MetaOrientationManager *self);
